1:[{"w":[0,"k","d"],"s":"fix2","c":"Token and tokenizer are different concepts","e":"Tokens may represent words, fragments, characters or bytes. Token IDs identify entries in a tokenizer vocabulary; the lesson uses invented IDs only for illustration.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/glossary"]},{"w":[1],"s":"fix2","c":"BPE is one algorithm, not an assumption about every tokenizer","e":"BPE learns adjacent merges; byte-level BPE starts from bytes. Average character ratios do not specify token boundaries.","u":["https://huggingface.co/learn/llm-course/en/chapter6/5"]},{"w":[1,2],"s":"fix2","c":"Count representative requests for the selected model","e":"The counting endpoint uses the selected model and returns an estimate. Do not transfer counts between tokenizer versions or treat a language multiplier as universal.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting"]}],
