5:[{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"With Anthropic, system is a separate top-level parameter, not a message in the array","e":"System prompt passed as top-level `system=` alongside `messages=[...]`; API ref lists `system` as its own parameter.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/system-prompts"]},{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"System holds persistent role/rules/format; user turn holds the per-turn request","e":"Role and general behaviour go in system; specific task instructions and data go in the user message.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/system-prompts"]},{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"Interpolating per-user data into system changes the prefix every request, so the cache never hits","e":"Cache hits 'require 100% identical prompt segments'; changing system invalidates system+messages caches. Cost guide: per-request status line in system cost $4.24 vs $0.59; 'Keep per-request text in the newest user turn'. (A tools-only breakpoint could still…","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching"]},{"w":[1],"s":"ok","c":"Instruction hierarchy: system > developer > user > tool results/retrieved content","e":"Model Spec: Root > System > Developer > User > Guideline; tool outputs, quoted text 'No Authority'. IH paper: System > User > ... > 'Text from tools'. Claude: operators > users; conversational inputs are 'information rather than commands'.","u":["https://model-spec.openai.com/2026-08-18.html"]},{"w":[1],"s":"ok","c":"Hierarchy is learned in instruction tuning and RLHF","e":"'fine-tune GPT-3.5 Turbo using supervised finetuning and reinforcement learning from human feedback' to 'selectively ignore lower-privileged instructions'.","u":["https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.13208"]},{"w":[2],"s":"ok","c":"It's a trained tendency, not an enforced boundary; no fool-proof prevention","e":"'it is unclear if there are fool-proof methods of prevention for prompt injection'; Anthropic: prompt injection 'is far from a solved problem'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":[2],"s":"ok","c":"Real controls outside the model: per-tool authorization, least privilege, output schema validation, human confirmation","e":"Mitigations: 'Define and validate expected output formats', 'Enforce privilege control and least privilege access', 'Require human approval for high-risk actions'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":[2],"s":"ok","c":"System prompts aren't secret; no keys or confidential logic in them","e":"'the system prompt should not be considered a secret, nor should it be used as a security control'; credentials 'should not be contained within the system prompt'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm072025-system-prompt-leakage/"]},{"w":["d"],"s":"ok","c":"Lie: system prompt is a hard boundary the model can't violate (must be false)","e":"System prompt shouldn't 'be used as a security control'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm072025-system-prompt-leakage/"]},{"w":["d"],"s":"ok","c":"Lie: per-user data belongs in the system prompt (must be false)","e":"Per-request text at the front of system broke the cache; 'keep per-request text in the newest user turn'. Anthropic also says third-party content goes in tool_result, 'never in system prompts'.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/optimizing-for-cost-and-intelligence"]}],
6:[{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"Prompt injection: untrusted text in context read as instruction rather than data","e":"Greshake et al.: 'LLM-Integrated Applications blur the line between data and instructions.'","u":["https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173"]},{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"Direct = user types the injection; indirect = instruction inside fetched web page/PDF/ticket","e":"Direct: 'a user's prompt input directly alters the behavior'; indirect: 'an LLM accepts input from external sources, such as websites or files.'","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":[0],"s":"ok","c":"Indirect injection is what threatens production agents","e":"Anthropic on browser agents: 'No browser agent is immune to prompt injection'; Opus 4.5 still 1% attack success vs adaptive attacker.","u":["https://www.anthropic.com/research/prompt-injection-defenses"]},{"w":[1],"s":"fix","c":"Mitigation: delimit untrusted content with tags and label it as data","e":"Anthropic: deliver third-party content 'inside tool_result blocks, never in system prompts or plain user text blocks'; JSON-encode so attacker 'cannot close a quote or tag to break out'.","u":["https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/test-and-evaluate/strengthen-guardrails/mitigate-jailbreaks"]},{"w":[1],"s":"ok","c":"Least privilege on every tool, human confirmation for destructive actions, schema-validate output, constrain agent reach","e":"'Enforce privilege control and least privilege access', 'Require human approval for high-risk actions', 'Define and validate expected output formats'; Anthropic: sandbox tools, 'scope permissions as narrowly as possible'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":[2],"s":"ok","c":"Delimiters raise attack cost but don't eliminate it; reliable boundary only in code outside the model","e":"'it is unclear if there are fool-proof methods of prevention'; Anthropic: prompt injection 'is far from a solved problem'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":["d"],"s":"ok","c":"Lie: prompt injection is only the user typing 'ignore previous instructions' (must be false)","e":"OWASP defines indirect injection from 'external sources, such as websites or files'.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]},{"w":["d"],"s":"ok","c":"Lie: good delimiters fully close the injection hole (must be false)","e":"No fool-proof prevention; Anthropic reports a non-zero attack success rate even with RL training and classifiers.","u":["https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]}],
